core-path-order

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Keep the person's PATH order when the core is already the first one found, so wrappers and shims ahead of the core's folder (such as a claude launcher in front of ~/.local/bin) still run in Herdr terminals.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream stops moving the core's folder ahead of PATH entries that do not hold another core.
